Use of Switch: 8/10 — The room, agent roles, permissions, approvals, and shared documents drive the workflow, though the checker can also run without Switch.

Technical execution: 7/10 — The write-up gives reproducible setup steps and describes tests and safeguards, but the code and demo are unavailable to verify those claims.

Creativity and impact: 8/10 — A human-approved, deterministic readiness gate addresses a practical team problem and gives agents distinct responsibilities.

Presentation and documentation: 6/10 — The README is detailed and clear, but the demo video is still “coming soon,” leaving the core workflow unshown.

Shortlist: Yes — The concept and documentation make a strong case, pending review of the code and demo.

Three biggest weaknesses:
1. No demo video is provided.
2. Technical claims, including the tests and gate behavior, cannot be verified from the written material alone.
3. The checker works without Switch, which weakens the claim that Switch is essential to the project.

TOTAL: 7.4
